<title>UK: BoE says dual maturity gilts mostly converted.</title>
<headline>BoE says dual maturity gilts mostly converted.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England's offer to convert holdings of a dual maturity gilt, due 2004/2008, into gilts due 2005, has been largely taken up, the Bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Of the 1.25 billion stg of the 13.5 percent, dual maturity gilts outstanding prior to the Bank's offer, 1.156 billion stg has been converted into the 8.5 percent stock due 2005, the Bank said.</p>
<p>The Bank said it will bid a price in line with current market prices for any amount of the dual maturity stock offered to it by gilt market makers.</p>
<p>-- Mike Peacock, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
